{"decision": "CONFIRM", "diagnosis": "Loopback with divider 64 sent 0xa5 but recv returned 0xe0, triggering TRAP: uart data mismatch got 0xe0 want 0xa5 and tohost FAIL 0xdead via simpleuart instance at picosoc/picosoc.v:190. Start-bit sync uses half-bit period (2*recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) but data-bit sampling at lines 90/97 uses (cfg_divider >> 4), 16x too fast. This early sampling shifts bits and corrupts 0xa5 to 0xe0; restoring full cfg_divider fixes the bit period.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -89,14 +89,14 @@
 				10: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_buf_data <= recv_pattern;
 						recv_buf_valid <= 1;
 						recv_state <= 0;
 					end
 				end
 				default: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_pattern <= {ser_rx, recv_pattern[7:1]};
 						recv_state <= recv_state + 1;
 						recv_divcnt <= 0;
 					end
 				end", "reason": "Diagram shows recv_divcnt threshold at 4 instead of 64 matching 16x early sampling that explains 0xa5 corrupting to 0xe0."}

